PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L02U3.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":2,"cefr":"A1b","unit":3,"theme":"Around My Town","essential_question":"How can we find our way and help others in our town?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1","title":"Turn Left at the Light: Giving Directions","objectives":["Students will be able to give directions with go straight, turn left/right and cross.","Students will be able to describe a place with between, opposite, near and on the corner.","I can give directions to a place.","I can say \"The bank is between the bakery and the park\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إعطاء الاتجاهات باستخدام go straight وturn left/right وcross.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف المكان باستخدام between وopposite وnear وon the corner.","أستطيع أن أعطي اتجاهات للوصول إلى مكان.","أستطيع أن أقول The bank is between the bakery and the park."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mosque","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mɑsk/","definition":"a building where Muslims pray","arabic":"مسجد","example":"The mosque is next to our school.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W01"},{"word":"hospital","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɑˌspɪtəl/","definition":"a building where doctors and nurses help sick people","arabic":"مستشفى","example":"My aunt works at the hospital.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W02"},{"word":"bank","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bæŋk/","definition":"a place where people keep their money","arabic":"بنك / مصرف","example":"Dad goes to the bank on Sunday.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W03"},{"word":"bakery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbeɪkɚi/","definition":"a shop that makes and sells bread and cakes","arabic":"مخبز","example":"The bakery smells wonderful.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To give directions, use imperatives (base verb, no subject): Go straight, Turn left, Turn right, Cross the street, Walk past the bank.\nTo say where a place is, use prepositions: between (in the middle of two places), opposite (across from, facing), near (close to), on the corner (where two streets meet).\nIn American English we often say across from for opposite: The park is across from the library.\nGo straight (on) • Turn left / right • Cross the street • Walk past …\nbetween A and B • opposite (across from) • near • next to • on the corner\nTurn left at the traffic light / at the corner.","examples":["Go straight for two blocks.","Turn right at the mosque.","Cross the street at the traffic light.","The bakery is between the bank and the pharmacy.","The hospital is opposite the park.","Our house is near the supermarket.","The café is on the corner of Palm Street.","Walk past the museum and stop at the bus stop."],"common_errors":["✗ You go straight and you turn left. → ✓ Go straight and turn left. (Directions use imperatives without you.)","✗ The bank is between the park with the school. → ✓ The bank is between the park and the school. (between … and …)","✗ Turn to left. → ✓ Turn left. (No to: turn left / turn right.)","✗ The park is in front the hospital. → ✓ The park is in front of / opposite the hospital. (Don't forget of.)"],"arabic":"نعطي الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر: Go straight (امشِ مستقيمًا) وTurn left (انعطف يسارًا) وCross the street (اعبر الشارع).\nbetween = بين (between … and …)، opposite = مقابل، near = قريب من، on the corner = على الزاوية.\nلا نقول Turn to left، بل Turn left."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Turn Left at the Light: Giving Directions”. Let’s learn imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U3-LS1 | Turn Left at the Light: Giving Directions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Where Is the Library?”: Adam: Excuse me. Where is the library, please? Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Adam: Excuse me. Where is the library, please?","visual":"Image GV-L02-U3-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To give directions, use imperatives (base verb, no subject): Go straight, Turn left, Turn right, Cross the street, Walk past the bank. To say where a place is, use prepositions: between (in the middle of two places), opposite (across from, facing), near (close to), on the corner (where two streets meet).","on_screen":"Go straight (on) • Turn left / right • Cross the street • Walk past … • between A and B • opposite (across from) • near • next to • on the corner • Turn left at the traffic light / at the corner.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Go straight for two blocks. Turn right at the mosque. Cross the street at the traffic light.","on_screen":"Go straight for two blocks. / Turn right at the mosque. / Cross the street at the traffic light.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You go straight and you turn left.” That’s not right. We say: “Go straight and turn left.” Directions use imperatives without you.","on_screen":"✗ You go straight and you turn left.   ✓ Go straight and turn left.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The bank is between the bakery and the park.\" How many places are next to the bank? … Think! … Two – the bakery and the park. Great job! Now you can say: I can give directions to a place.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give directions to a place.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نعطي الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر: Go straight (امشِ مستقيمًا) وTurn left (انعطف يسارًا) وCross the street (اعبر الشارع).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You go straight and you turn left. — الصحيح: Go straight and turn left.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعطي اتجاهات للوصول إلى مكان."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Where Is the Library?","body":"Adam: Excuse me. Where is the library, please?\nOfficer: Go straight along King Fahd Street. Turn left at the traffic light.\nAdam: Turn left at the traffic light. OK.\nOfficer: Walk past the hospital. The library is between the bank and the bakery. It's opposite the park.\nAdam: Is there a bus stop near the library?\nOfficer: Yes, there is. It's on the corner, next to the mosque.\nAdam: Thank you very much!\nOfficer: You're welcome.","word_count":76,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Look at the town map. Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The library is ___ the bank and the bakery.","options":["under","between","on","opposite"],"answer":"between","explanation":"between A and B.","explanation_ar":"between ثم المكان الأول ثم and ثم الثاني."},{"q":"The park is ___ the library. It's on the other side of the street.","options":["between","under","in","opposite"],"answer":"opposite","explanation":"opposite / across from = facing on the other side.","explanation_ar":"opposite تعني مقابل."},{"q":"___ left at the traffic light.","options":["Turns","Turn","You turn","Turning"],"answer":"Turn","explanation":"Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"The pharmacy is ___ the corner.","options":["in","at the","on","under"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on the corner = where two streets meet.","explanation_ar":"on the corner تعني على الزاوية."},{"q":"The bus stop is ___ the mosque. It's close.","options":["near","between","under","opposite of"],"answer":"near","explanation":"near = close to.","explanation_ar":"near تعني قريب من."},{"q":"___ the street at the green light.","options":["Crosses","Crossing","Cross","You crosses"],"answer":"Cross","explanation":"Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete the directions. Word bank: and, Go, right","items":[{"q":"______ straight along the street.","options":[],"answer":"Go","explanation":"Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"Turn ______ at the bank.","options":[],"answer":"right","explanation":"Turn left/right – no to.","explanation_ar":"نقول Turn left بدون to."},{"q":"The bakery is between the bank ______ the park.","options":[],"answer":"and","explanation":"between A and B.","explanation_ar":"between ثم المكان الأول ثم and ثم الثاني."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"mosque / The / is / opposite / the / hospital   ( . )","options":["mosque","The","is","opposite","the","hospital"],"answer":"The mosque is opposite the hospital.","explanation":"Word order: opposite / across from = facing on the other side.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: opposite تعني مقابل."},{"q":"at / left / the / Turn / corner   ( . )","options":["at","left","the","Turn","corner"],"answer":"Turn left at the corner.","explanation":"Word order: Turn left/right – no to.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: نقول Turn left بدون to."},{"q":"museum / the / past / Walk   ( . )","options":["museum","the","past","Walk"],"answer":"Walk past the museum.","explanation":"Word order: Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about places in your town.","items":[{"q":"My school is near ___.","options":[],"answer":"My school is near a big mosque.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The supermarket is opposite ___.","options":[],"answer":"The supermarket is opposite the bank.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"There is a ___ on the corner of my street.","options":[],"answer":"There is a bakery on the corner of my street.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My house is between ___ and ___.","options":[],"answer":"My house is between my uncle's house and a park.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"To go from school to the shop, turn ___.","options":[],"answer":"To go from school to the shop, turn right.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Draw and give directions.","items":[{"q":"Draw a simple map of your street with 4 places. Write where they are.","options":[],"answer":"The mosque is on the corner. The bakery is next to the mosque. The park is opposite the bakery.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write directions from your school to the nearest shop (3 steps).","options":[],"answer":"Go straight. Turn left at the traffic light. The shop is on the right.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Give your directions to a partner. Write if he arrives at the right place.","options":[],"answer":"Yes, he finds the shop.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"the bank"},{"label":"the park"},{"label":"the mosque"},{"label":"the bakery"},{"label":"the hospital"},{"label":"the library"},{"label":"the bus stop"},{"label":"the museum"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The bank is ___ the café and the school.","options":["on","in front","between","opposite"],"answer":"between","explanation":"between A and B.","explanation_ar":"between ثم المكان الأول ثم and ثم الثاني."},{"q":"The mosque is ___ the park. They face each other.","options":["between","in","opposite","under"],"answer":"opposite","explanation":"opposite / across from = facing on the other side.","explanation_ar":"opposite تعني مقابل."},{"q":"___ straight for two minutes.","options":["Go","Going","You goes","Goes"],"answer":"Go","explanation":"Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["Turn right at the hospital.","Turns right at the hospital.","You turning right at the hospital.","Turn to right at the hospital."],"answer":"Turn right at the hospital.","explanation":"Turn left/right – no to.","explanation_ar":"نقول Turn left بدون to."},{"q":"","options":["The bakery between is the bank and the park.","The bakery is between the bank with the park.","The bakery is between of the bank and the park.","The bakery is between the bank and the park."],"answer":"The bakery is between the bank and the park.","explanation":"between A and B.","explanation_ar":"between ثم المكان الأول ثم and ثم الثاني."},{"q":"The pharmacy is ___ the corner of Palm Street.","options":["between","on","in","opposite of"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on the corner = where two streets meet.","explanation_ar":"on the corner تعني على الزاوية."},{"q":"Our house is ___ the school. We walk there in two minutes.","options":["opposite of","near","under","between"],"answer":"near","explanation":"near = close to.","explanation_ar":"near تعني قريب من."},{"q":"","options":["You walk past the library and you cross the street.","Walks past the library and crosses the street.","Walk past the library and cross the street.","Walking past the library and crossing the street."],"answer":"Walk past the library and cross the street.","explanation":"Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"In American English, \"opposite\" can also be ___.","options":["between","next to of","on top","across from"],"answer":"across from","explanation":"opposite / across from = facing on the other side.","explanation_ar":"opposite تعني مقابل."},{"q":"The hospital is opposite the park. Where is the park?","options":["inside the hospital","on the hospital","behind the hospital","across from the hospital"],"answer":"across from the hospital","explanation":"opposite / across from = facing on the other side.","explanation_ar":"opposite تعني مقابل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Adam on a town street holding a map, asking a friendly police officer for directions; a library, bank and bakery in a row and a park across the street. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam on a town street holding a map, asking a friendly police officer for directions; a library, bank and bakery in a row and a park across the street"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mosque (a building where Muslims pray); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mosque: a building where Muslims pray"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hospital (a building where doctors and nurses help sick people); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hospital: a building where doctors and nurses help sick people"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bank (a place where people keep their money); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bank: a place where people keep their money"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bakery (a shop that makes and sells bread and cakes); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bakery: a shop that makes and sells bread and cakes"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W01","script":"mosque. mosque. The mosque is next to our school.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W02","script":"hospital. hospital. My aunt works at the hospital.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W03","script":"bank. bank. Dad goes to the bank on Sunday.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-W04","script":"bakery. bakery. The bakery smells wonderful.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-T1","script":"Adam: Excuse me. Where is the library, please? Officer: Go straight along King Fahd Street. Turn left at the traffic light. Adam: Turn left at the traffic light. OK. Officer: Walk past the hospital. The library is between the bank and the bakery. It's opposite the park. Adam: Is there a bus stop near the library? Officer: Yes, there is. It's on the corner, next to the mosque. Adam: Thank you very much! Officer: You're welcome.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Turn Left at the Light: Giving Directions”. Let’s learn imperatives for directions + prepositions between, opposite, near, on the corner together. Listen to the start of “Where Is the Library?”: Adam: Excuse me. Where is the library, please? Look at the green words. To give directions, use imperatives (base verb, no subject): Go straight, Turn left, Turn right, Cross the street, Walk past the bank. To say where a place is, use prepositions: between (in the middle of two places), opposite (across from, facing), near (close to), on the corner (where two streets meet). Here are some examples. Go straight for two blocks. Turn right at the mosque. Cross the street at the traffic light. Be careful! Some learners say: “You go straight and you turn left.” That’s not right. We say: “Go straight and turn left.” Directions use imperatives without you. Quick check: \"The bank is between the bakery and the park.\" How many places are next to the bank? … Think! … Two – the bakery and the park. Great job! Now you can say: I can give directions to a place.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2","title":"Excuse Me, Is There a Bank Near Here?","objectives":["Students will be able to ask polite questions about places with Where is…? and Is there…?","Students will be able to answer questions about places with short answers and directions.","I can ask \"Excuse me, is there a bakery near here?\"","I can ask \"How do I get to the park?\" and understand the answer."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة مهذبة عن الأماكن باستخدام Where is…? وIs there…?","سيتمكن الطلاب من الإجابة بإجابات قصيرة واتجاهات.","أستطيع أن أسأل Excuse me, is there a bakery near here?","أستطيع أن أسأل How do I get to the park? وأفهم الإجابة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"supermarket","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsupɚˌmɑrkɪt/","definition":"a big shop that sells food and other things","arabic":"سوبرماركت","example":"We buy milk at the supermarket.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W01"},{"word":"park","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɑrk/","definition":"a public garden where people walk and play","arabic":"حديقة عامة","example":"Children play on the swings in the park.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W02"},{"word":"library","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlaɪbrɛˌri/","definition":"a place with many books you can borrow","arabic":"مكتبة عامة","example":"The library has a quiet reading room.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W03"},{"word":"museum","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mjuˈziəm/","definition":"a building where you can see old or interesting things","arabic":"متحف","example":"We see old coins at the museum.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Start politely with Excuse me. Then ask: Where is the bank? / Is there a bakery near here? / How do I get to the park?\nAnswer Is there…? with Yes, there is. / No, there isn't. Then give directions or say where it is.\nSay Thank you or Thanks at the end, and answer You're welcome.","examples":["Excuse me, where is the post office?","Is there a pharmacy near here? – Yes, there is.","How do I get to the museum? – Take bus number 5.","Are there any restaurants on this street? – No, there aren't.","Where's the nearest bus stop? – It's on the corner.","Is the park far from here? – No, it's very close.","Thank you! – You're welcome.","Excuse me, which way is the mosque? – It's that way, on your right."],"common_errors":["✗ Where the bank is? → ✓ Where is the bank? (In a question, is comes before the place.)","✗ Have a bakery near here? → ✓ Is there a bakery near here? (Use Is there, not Have.)","✗ How I go to the park? → ✓ How do I get to the park? (Use How do I get to…?)","✗ Hey you! Where is the bank? → ✓ Excuse me, where is the bank? (Start politely.)"],"arabic":"نبدأ السؤال بأدب: Excuse me.\nنسأل Where is…? (أين…؟) وIs there… near here? (هل يوجد… قريبًا من هنا؟) وHow do I get to…? (كيف أصل إلى…؟).\nلا نقول Have a bank near here?، بل Is there a bank near here?\nنقول Thank you ويجيب الآخر You're welcome (عفوًا)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Excuse Me, Is There a Bank Near Here?”. Let’s learn asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U3-LS2 | Excuse Me, Is There a Bank Near Here?","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: There's a bakery near here. It's on Rose Street. There isn't a museum near here. • There aren't any banks on this street. Excuse me, where is the hospital? • Is there a supermarket near here? – Yes, there is. • How do I get to the library? – Go straight and turn right.","on_screen":"There's a bakery near here. It's on Rose Street. | There isn't a museum near here. • There aren't any banks on this street. | Excuse me, where is the hospital? • Is there a supermarket near here? – Yes, there is. • How do I get to the library? – Go straight and turn right.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Start politely with Excuse me. Then ask: Where is the bank? / Is there a bakery near here? / How do I get to the park? Answer Is there…? with Yes, there is. / No, there isn't. Then give directions or say where it is.","on_screen":"asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Excuse me, where is the post office? Is there a pharmacy near here? – Yes, there is. How do I get to the museum? – Take bus number 5.","on_screen":"Excuse me, where is the post office? / Is there a pharmacy near here? – Yes, there is. / How do I get to the museum? – Take bus number 5.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Where the bank is?.” That’s not right. We say: “Where is the bank?.” In a question, is comes before the place.","on_screen":"✗ Where the bank is?   ✓ Where is the bank?","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What do we say before we ask a stranger a question? … Think! … *Excuse me.* Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"Excuse me, is there a bakery near here?\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can ask \"Excuse me, is there a bakery near here?\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…?.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نبدأ السؤال بأدب: Excuse me.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Where the bank is? — الصحيح: Where is the bank?","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسأل Excuse me, is there a bakery near here?"]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___, where is the bus stop?","options":["You're welcome","Excuse me","Goodbye","Thank you"],"answer":"Excuse me","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."},{"q":"___ a hospital near here?","options":["There is","Are there","Have","Is there"],"answer":"Is there","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"Is there a bank on this street? – Yes, there ___.","options":["has","is","have","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"___ the museum? – It's next to the park.","options":["Where","How","Where is","Is there"],"answer":"Where is","explanation":"Where is + place?","explanation_ar":"Where is ثم المكان."},{"q":"How do I ___ to the library?","options":["to get","getting","gets","get"],"answer":"get","explanation":"How do I get to + place?","explanation_ar":"How do I get to للسؤال عن الطريق."},{"q":"Thank you for your help! – ___","options":["You're welcome.","Excuse me.","Yes, there is.","Turn left."],"answer":"You're welcome.","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions.","items":[{"q":"the bakery  (Where)","options":[],"answer":"Where is the bakery?","explanation":"Where is + place?","explanation_ar":"Where is ثم المكان."},{"q":"a pharmacy / near here  (Is there)","options":[],"answer":"Is there a pharmacy near here?","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"the park  (How)","options":[],"answer":"How do I get to the park?","explanation":"How do I get to + place?","explanation_ar":"How do I get to للسؤال عن الطريق."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete the dialogue. Word bank: welcome, Excuse, is","items":[{"q":"A: ______ me, is there a mosque near here?","options":[],"answer":"Excuse","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."},{"q":"B: Yes, there ______. It's on Al-Noor Street.","options":[],"answer":"is","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"A: Thank you! B: You're ______.","options":[],"answer":"welcome","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about your town.","items":[{"q":"Is there a pharmacy near your house?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, there is. It's opposite my house.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Where is the nearest supermarket?","options":[],"answer":"It's on the corner of my street.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How do you get to school?","options":[],"answer":"I go straight and turn right at the mosque.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Is there a museum in your town?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, there is. It's near the castle.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Where is your favorite place in town?","options":[],"answer":"My favorite place is the park near the lake.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Role-play: tourist and helper.","items":[{"q":"Write a 6-line dialogue between a tourist and a helper.","options":[],"answer":"A: Excuse me, is there a bakery near here? B: Yes, there is. A: How do I get there? B: Go straight and turn left. A: Thank you! B: You're welcome.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Act it out with a partner. Write one new question your partner asks.","options":[],"answer":"Is there a bus stop near the bakery?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 polite phrases you use when you ask for help.","options":[],"answer":"Excuse me. Thank you very much.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…?.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"Where / the bank / ?"},{"cue":"Is there / a bakery / ?"},{"cue":"the park / opposite / the school"},{"cue":"the mosque / between / the bank and the shop"},{"cue":"Turn / left / at the light"},{"cue":"Go / straight / for two blocks"},{"cue":"Is there / a bus stop / ?"},{"cue":"the museum / near / the river"},{"cue":"Where / the library / ?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___, is there a pharmacy near here?","options":["Turn left","Goodbye","Excuse me","You're welcome"],"answer":"Excuse me","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."},{"q":"","options":["Is a bakery there on this street?","Is there a bakery on this street?","Have a bakery on this street?","There is a bakery on this street?"],"answer":"Is there a bakery on this street?","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"Is there a library near the school? – No, there ___.","options":["doesn't","isn't","aren't","not"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"","options":["The hospital where is?","Where the hospital is?","Where is hospital the?","Where is the hospital?"],"answer":"Where is the hospital?","explanation":"Where is + place?","explanation_ar":"Where is ثم المكان."},{"q":"","options":["How do I get to the bank?","How do I gets to the bank?","How I do get to the bank?","How I get to the bank?"],"answer":"How do I get to the bank?","explanation":"How do I get to + place?","explanation_ar":"How do I get to للسؤال عن الطريق."},{"q":"___ any cafés on this road? – Yes, there are two.","options":["Have","Is there","There are","Are there"],"answer":"Are there","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"Thank you so much! – ___","options":["Go straight.","Excuse me.","You're welcome.","No, there isn't."],"answer":"You're welcome.","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."},{"q":"Where's the post office? – ___","options":["It opposite the bank.","It's opposite the bank.","Yes, there is.","Turn on left."],"answer":"It's opposite the bank.","explanation":"Where is + place?","explanation_ar":"Where is ثم المكان."},{"q":"","options":["Excuse me, where way is the museum?","Excuse me, which is way the museum?","Excuse me, which way the museum is?","Excuse me, which way is the museum?"],"answer":"Excuse me, which way is the museum?","explanation":"Where is + place?","explanation_ar":"Where is ثم المكان."},{"q":"How do I get to the mall? – ___","options":["Take bus number 7.","No, there aren't.","Yes, it is.","It's welcome."],"answer":"Take bus number 7.","explanation":"How do I get to + place?","explanation_ar":"How do I get to للسؤال عن الطريق."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Sara and her mother in a busy town square asking a shopkeeper for directions; signs for a bank, bakery and supermarket around them. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara and her mother in a busy town square asking a shopkeeper for directions; signs for a bank, bakery and supermarket around them"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Around My Town”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Around My Town”"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows supermarket (a big shop that sells food and other things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing supermarket: a big shop that sells food and other things"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows park (a public garden where people walk and play); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing park: a public garden where people walk and play"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows library (a place with many books you can borrow); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing library: a place with many books you can borrow"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows museum (a building where you can see old or interesting things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing museum: a building where you can see old or interesting things"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W01","script":"supermarket. supermarket. We buy milk at the supermarket.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W02","script":"park. park. Children play on the swings in the park.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W03","script":"library. library. The library has a quiet reading room.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-W04","script":"museum. museum. We see old coins at the museum.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Excuse Me, Is There a Bank Near Here?”. Let’s learn asking for directions: Where is…? Is there a … near here? How do I get to…? together. Remember these patterns: There's a bakery near here. It's on Rose Street. There isn't a museum near here. • There aren't any banks on this street. Excuse me, where is the hospital? • Is there a supermarket near here? – Yes, there is. • How do I get to the library? – Go straight and turn right. Start politely with Excuse me. Then ask: Where is the bank? / Is there a bakery near here? / How do I get to the park? Answer Is there…? with Yes, there is. / No, there isn't. Then give directions or say where it is. Here are some examples. Excuse me, where is the post office? Is there a pharmacy near here? – Yes, there is. How do I get to the museum? – Take bus number 5. Be careful! Some learners say: “Where the bank is?.” That’s not right. We say: “Where is the bank?.” In a question, is comes before the place. Quick check: What do we say before we ask a stranger a question? … Think! … *Excuse me.* Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"Excuse me, is there a bakery near here?\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3","title":"Places in Town: Compound Nouns","objectives":["Students will be able to name places in a town and what people do there.","Students will be able to understand and use two-word compound nouns.","I can name places in my town and say what we do there.","I can use words like \"bus stop\" and \"post office\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية الأماكن في المدينة وما يفعله الناس فيها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من فهم الأسماء المركبة من كلمتين واستخدامها.","أستطيع أن أسمّي أماكن مدينتي وأقول ماذا نفعل فيها.","أستطيع أن أستخدم كلمات مثل bus stop وpost office."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"bus stop","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bʌs stɑp/","definition":"a place where the bus stops for people","arabic":"موقف الحافلات","example":"Wait at the bus stop, please.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W01"},{"word":"street","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strit/","definition":"a road in a town with buildings on each side","arabic":"شارع","example":"Our street has tall palm trees.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W02"},{"word":"corner","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɔrnɚ/","definition":"the place where two streets meet","arabic":"زاوية / ناصية","example":"The pharmacy is on the corner.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W03"},{"word":"traffic light","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtræfɪk laɪt/","definition":"red, yellow and green lights that control cars","arabic":"إشارة المرور","example":"Stop at the red traffic light.","image_id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Every place in town has a job: we borrow books at the library, we buy bread at the bakery, doctors help sick people at the hospital.\nMany place names are compound nouns made of two words: bus + stop = bus stop; post + office = post office. The first word tells us what kind: a fire station is a station for fire trucks.\nUse the when you talk about a place everyone knows in your town: I go to the bank.\nCollocations/phrases: bus stop • post office • police station • fire station • shopping mall • traffic light • parking lot (US) | library → borrow books • bakery → buy bread • bank → keep money • hospital → see a doctor • mosque → pray | park → play and walk • museum → see old things • supermarket → buy food","examples":["We wait for the bus at the bus stop.","Firefighters work at the fire station.","My dad sends letters from the post office.","We borrow books from the library.","The museum has old swords and coins.","Grandma buys fresh bread at the bakery.","The parking lot is full on Friday.","People keep their money in a bank."],"common_errors":["✗ I borrow books from the bookshop. → ✓ I borrow books from the library. (We buy books at a bookshop and borrow them from a library.)","✗ the station of police → ✓ the police station (In compound nouns, the \"kind\" word comes first.)","✗ I go to hospital to buy bread. → ✓ I go to the bakery to buy bread. (Use the place that matches the action.)"],"arabic":"كل مكان في المدينة له وظيفة: library (مكتبة للاستعارة)، bakery (مخبز)، hospital (مستشفى).\nكثير من أسماء الأماكن مركبة من كلمتين: bus stop (موقف الحافلات)، police station (مركز الشرطة).\nفي الإنجليزية تأتي كلمة النوع أولًا: police station وليس station police."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Places in Town: Compound Nouns”. Let’s learn places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U3-LS3 | Places in Town: Compound Nouns","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. bus stop: a place where the bus stops for people. street: a road in a town with buildings on each side. corner: the place where two streets meet.","on_screen":"bus stop | street | corner","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Every place in town has a job: we borrow books at the library, we buy bread at the bakery, doctors help sick people at the hospital. Many place names are compound nouns made of two words: bus + stop = bus stop; post + office = post office. The first word tells us what kind: a fire station is a station for fire trucks.","on_screen":"places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We wait for the bus at the bus stop. Firefighters work at the fire station. My dad sends letters from the post office.","on_screen":"We wait for the bus at the bus stop. / Firefighters work at the fire station. / My dad sends letters from the post office.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I borrow books from the bookshop.” That’s not right. We say: “I borrow books from the library.” We buy books at a bookshop and borrow them from a library.","on_screen":"✗ I borrow books from the bookshop.   ✓ I borrow books from the library.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we buy books or borrow books at a library? … Think! … We *borrow* books. Great job! Now you can say: I can name places in my town and say what we do there.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name places in my town and say what we do there.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كل مكان في المدينة له وظيفة: library (مكتبة للاستعارة)، bakery (مخبز)، hospital (مستشفى).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I borrow books from the bookshop. — الصحيح: I borrow books from the library.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي أماكن مدينتي وأقول ماذا نفعل فيها."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"We see a doctor at the ___.","options":["bank","hospital","library","bakery"],"answer":"hospital","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"We borrow books from the ___.","options":["museum","bakery","library","bank"],"answer":"library","explanation":"borrow = take and give back later; buy = pay money.","explanation_ar":"borrow تعني يستعير."},{"q":"Firefighters work at the ___.","options":["station fire","bus stop","post office","fire station"],"answer":"fire station","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"We buy fresh bread at the ___.","options":["museum","bakery","bank","mosque"],"answer":"bakery","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"We wait for the bus at the ___.","options":["bus stop","traffic light","bus station office","stop bus"],"answer":"bus stop","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"We see old coins and swords at the ___.","options":["park","bakery","museum","supermarket"],"answer":"museum","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the place to the activity.","items":[{"q":"mosque","options":["walk and play","ask the police for help","buy food","keep money safe","send letters","pray"],"answer":"pray","explanation":"mosque → pray. Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"bank","options":["walk and play","ask the police for help","buy food","keep money safe","send letters","pray"],"answer":"keep money safe","explanation":"bank → keep money safe. Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"park","options":["walk and play","ask the police for help","buy food","keep money safe","send letters","pray"],"answer":"walk and play","explanation":"park → walk and play. Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"post office","options":["walk and play","ask the police for help","buy food","keep money safe","send letters","pray"],"answer":"send letters","explanation":"post office → send letters. Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"supermarket","options":["walk and play","ask the police for help","buy food","keep money safe","send letters","pray"],"answer":"buy food","explanation":"supermarket → buy food. Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"police station","options":["walk and play","ask the police for help","buy food","keep money safe","send letters","pray"],"answer":"ask the police for help","explanation":"police station → ask the police for help. Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about places in your town.","items":[{"q":"In my town, there is a ___. People ___ there.","options":[],"answer":"In my town, there is a big library. People read and borrow books there.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I go to the ___ with my family on Friday.","options":[],"answer":"I go to the park with my family on Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite place in town is the ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite place in town is the museum.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I don't like going to the ___ because ___.","options":[],"answer":"I don't like going to the dentist because I am scared.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Make a compound noun: shopping + ___ = ___","options":[],"answer":"shopping + mall = shopping mall","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a \"My Town\" guide.","items":[{"q":"Draw 4 places in your town. Write what people do in each one.","options":[],"answer":"library – borrow books; bakery – buy bread; park – play; mosque – pray","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences for a visitor about your town.","options":[],"answer":"There is a big park near the lake. The museum is interesting. The bakery on King Faisal Street is delicious.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 compound nouns for places and draw them.","options":[],"answer":"bus stop, fire station, post office","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"mosque","match":"a building where Muslims pray","arabic":"مسجد"},{"word":"hospital","match":"a building where doctors and nurses help sick people","arabic":"مستشفى"},{"word":"bank","match":"a place where people keep their money","arabic":"بنك / مصرف"},{"word":"bakery","match":"a shop that makes and sells bread and cakes","arabic":"مخبز"},{"word":"supermarket","match":"a big shop that sells food and other things","arabic":"سوبرماركت"},{"word":"park","match":"a public garden where people walk and play","arabic":"حديقة عامة"},{"word":"library","match":"a place with many books you can borrow","arabic":"مكتبة عامة"},{"word":"museum","match":"a building where you can see old or interesting things","arabic":"متحف"},{"word":"bus stop","match":"a place where the bus stops for people","arabic":"موقف الحافلات"},{"word":"street","match":"a road in a town with buildings on each side","arabic":"شارع"},{"word":"corner","match":"the place where two streets meet","arabic":"زاوية / ناصية"},{"word":"traffic light","match":"red, yellow and green lights that control cars","arabic":"إشارة المرور"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We pray at the ___.","options":["museum","bakery","bank","mosque"],"answer":"mosque","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"We keep money in the ___.","options":["park","library","bank","bakery"],"answer":"bank","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"The police work at the ___.","options":["police station","post office","station police","fire stop"],"answer":"police station","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"We send a letter at the ___.","options":["office post","post office","bus stop","fire station"],"answer":"post office","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"Children play on the swings at the ___.","options":["hospital","bank","post office","park"],"answer":"park","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"Which is a compound noun?","options":["light","traffic","traffic light","street"],"answer":"traffic light","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"I ___ two books from the library every week.","options":["pay","sell","buy","borrow"],"answer":"borrow","explanation":"borrow = take and give back later; buy = pay money.","explanation_ar":"borrow تعني يستعير."},{"q":"We park our car in the ___.","options":["parking lot","bus stop","lot parking","post office"],"answer":"parking lot","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"We buy food and drinks at the ___.","options":["museum","supermarket","library","mosque"],"answer":"supermarket","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"A doctor works at a ___.","options":["bank","bakery","hospital","fire station"],"answer":"hospital","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A colorful town map with small buildings: a mosque, hospital, police station, fire station, post office, bakery, library, park and a bus stop. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A colorful town map with small buildings: a mosque, hospital, police station, fire station, post office, bakery, library, park and a bus stop"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bus stop (a place where the bus stops for people); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bus stop: a place where the bus stops for people"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows street (a road in a town with buildings on each side); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing street: a road in a town with buildings on each side"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows corner (the place where two streets meet); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing corner: the place where two streets meet"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows traffic light (red, yellow and green lights that control cars); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing traffic light: red, yellow and green lights that control cars"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W01","script":"bus stop. bus stop. Wait at the bus stop, please.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W02","script":"street. street. Our street has tall palm trees.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W03","script":"corner. corner. The pharmacy is on the corner.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-W04","script":"traffic light. traffic light. Stop at the red traffic light.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Places in Town: Compound Nouns”. Let’s learn places in town; two-word compound nouns (bus stop, post office, police station) together. Meet some new words. bus stop: a place where the bus stops for people. street: a road in a town with buildings on each side. corner: the place where two streets meet. Every place in town has a job: we borrow books at the library, we buy bread at the bakery, doctors help sick people at the hospital. Many place names are compound nouns made of two words: bus + stop = bus stop; post + office = post office. The first word tells us what kind: a fire station is a station for fire trucks. Here are some examples. We wait for the bus at the bus stop. Firefighters work at the fire station. My dad sends letters from the post office. Be careful! Some learners say: “I borrow books from the bookshop.” That’s not right. We say: “I borrow books from the library.” We buy books at a bookshop and borrow them from a library. Quick check: Do we buy books or borrow books at a library? … Think! … We *borrow* books. Great job! Now you can say: I can name places in my town and say what we do there.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4","title":"Capital Letters for Places","objectives":["Students will be able to capitalize the names of cities, countries, streets and buildings.","Students will be able to tell the difference between a common noun (street) and a proper noun (Palm Street).","I can write \"Taif\", \"Saudi Arabia\" and \"King Fahd Street\" with capital letters.","I can see the difference between \"my street\" and \"Palm Street\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة أسماء المدن والدول والشوارع والمباني بحرف كبير.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التمييز بين الاسم العام (street) واسم العلم (Palm Street).","أستطيع أن أكتب Taif وSaudi Arabia وKing Fahd Street بحروف كبيرة.","أستطيع أن أميّز بين my street وPalm Street."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mosque","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mɑsk/","definition":"a building where Muslims pray","arabic":"مسجد","example":"The mosque is next to our school.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hospital","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɑˌspɪtəl/","definition":"a building where doctors and nurses help sick people","arabic":"مستشفى","example":"My aunt works at the hospital.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bank","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bæŋk/","definition":"a place where people keep their money","arabic":"بنك / مصرف","example":"Dad goes to the bank on Sunday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bakery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbeɪkɚi/","definition":"a shop that makes and sells bread and cakes","arabic":"مخبز","example":"The bakery smells wonderful.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"supermarket","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsupɚˌmɑrkɪt/","definition":"a big shop that sells food and other things","arabic":"سوبرماركت","example":"We buy milk at the supermarket.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"park","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɑrk/","definition":"a public garden where people walk and play","arabic":"حديقة عامة","example":"Children play on the swings in the park.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A proper noun is the special name of one place. It starts with a capital letter: Taif, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, King Fahd Street, Al-Noor Mosque.\nA common noun is a general word: city, street, mosque, park. It does not need a capital letter: I live on a quiet street.\nWhen the common word is part of the name, it gets a capital too: Palm Street, Taif Museum, King Fahd Hospital.\nCities and countries → capitals: Jeddah, Egypt\nStreets and roads with names → capitals: Rose Street, Al-Hada Road\nNamed buildings and parks → capitals: King Abdullah Park\nGeneral words → small letters: a big city, my street, the hospital","examples":["I live in Taif.","My cousins live in Jeddah, near the sea.","We go to King Abdullah Park on Friday.","The bakery is on Rose Street.","Saudi Arabia is a big country.","Our street has many palm trees.","My uncle works at King Fahd Hospital.","The museum is near the old market."],"common_errors":["✗ I live in taif. → ✓ I live in Taif. (City names need a capital letter.)","✗ We visit king abdullah park. → ✓ We visit King Abdullah Park. (Every word in the name has a capital.)","✗ My House is on a quiet Street. → ✓ My house is on a quiet street. (General words are small letters.)"],"arabic":"أسماء العلم (المدن والدول والشوارع والمباني) تبدأ بحرف كبير: Taif وSaudi Arabia.\nالأسماء العامة مثل street وcity وpark تُكتب بحرف صغير.\nعندما تكون الكلمة العامة جزءًا من الاسم تُكتب بحرف كبير: Palm Street."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Capital Letters for Places”. Let’s learn capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U3-LS4 | Capital Letters for Places","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A proper noun is the special name of one place. It starts with a capital letter: Taif, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, King Fahd Street, Al-Noor Mosque.","on_screen":"capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A proper noun is the special name of one place. It starts with a capital letter: Taif, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, King Fahd Street, Al-Noor Mosque. A common noun is a general word: city, street, mosque, park. It does not need a capital letter: I live on a quiet street.","on_screen":"Cities and countries → capitals: Jeddah, Egypt • Streets and roads with names → capitals: Rose Street, Al-Hada Road • Named buildings and parks → capitals: King Abdullah Park","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I live in Taif. My cousins live in Jeddah, near the sea. We go to King Abdullah Park on Friday.","on_screen":"I live in Taif. / My cousins live in Jeddah, near the sea. / We go to King Abdullah Park on Friday.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I live in taif.” That’s not right. We say: “I live in Taif.” City names need a capital letter.","on_screen":"✗ I live in taif.   ✓ I live in Taif.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Does \"street\" need a capital in \"I live on a long street\"? … Think! … No – it is a common noun. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Taif\", \"Saudi Arabia\" and \"King Fahd Street\" with capital letters.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"Taif\", \"Saudi Arabia\" and \"King Fahd Street\" with capital letters.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","أسماء العلم (المدن والدول والشوارع والمباني) تبدأ بحرف كبير: Taif وSaudi Arabia.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I live in taif. — الصحيح: I live in Taif.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب Taif وSaudi Arabia وKing Fahd Street بحروف كبيرة."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Postcard from Abha (editing passage)","body":"dear Yusuf, I am in abha with my family. Our hotel is on king Khalid Road. Today we go to a big Park in the mountains. Tomorrow we visit jeddah. See you soon! Adam","word_count":34,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["My aunt lives in Riyadh.","My Aunt lives in riyadh.","My aunt lives in riyadh.","my aunt lives in Riyadh."],"answer":"My aunt lives in Riyadh.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["We walk in king Fahd Park.","We walk in king fahd park.","We walk in King fahd park.","We walk in King Fahd Park."],"answer":"We walk in King Fahd Park.","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["our school is on a busy street.","Our School is on a busy Street.","Our school is on a busy street.","Our school is on a busy Street."],"answer":"Our school is on a busy street.","explanation":"General place words (street, city, park) are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["Egypt and Jordan are near Saudi Arabia.","egypt and jordan are near saudi arabia.","Egypt and Jordan are near saudi Arabia.","Egypt and jordan are near Saudi arabia."],"answer":"Egypt and Jordan are near Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["the museum is next to a park.","The museum is next to a park.","The Museum is next to a Park.","The museum is next to a Park."],"answer":"The museum is next to a park.","explanation":"General place words (street, city, park) are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["Grandpa's house is on Al-Hada road.","Grandpa's house is on Al-Hada Road.","grandpa's house is on Al-Hada Road.","Grandpa's house is on al-hada road."],"answer":"Grandpa's house is on Al-Hada Road.","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the capital letter mistake.","items":[{"q":"My cousin goes to school in makkah.","options":[],"answer":"My cousin goes to school in Makkah.","explanation":"makkah → Makkah. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: makkah → Makkah. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"The bakery is on palm Street.","options":[],"answer":"The bakery is on Palm Street.","explanation":"palm → Palm. Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: palm → Palm. كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"There is a big Mosque near my house.","options":[],"answer":"There is a big mosque near my house.","explanation":"Mosque → mosque. General place words (street, city, park) are small letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Mosque → mosque. الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"We fly to malaysia in summer.","options":[],"answer":"We fly to Malaysia in summer.","explanation":"malaysia → Malaysia. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: malaysia → Malaysia. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"King Faisal hospital is very big.","options":[],"answer":"King Faisal Hospital is very big.","explanation":"hospital → Hospital. Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: hospital → Hospital. كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"My friend lives in a small Town.","options":[],"answer":"My friend lives in a small town.","explanation":"Town → town. General place words (street, city, park) are small letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Town → town. الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit Adam's postcard.","items":[{"q":"dear Yusuf, I am in Abha with my family.","options":[],"answer":"Dear Yusuf, I am in Abha with my family.","explanation":"dear → Dear. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: dear → Dear. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Dear Yusuf, I am in abha with my family.","options":[],"answer":"Dear Yusuf, I am in Abha with my family.","explanation":"abha → Abha. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: abha → Abha. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Our hotel is on king Khalid Road.","options":[],"answer":"Our hotel is on King Khalid Road.","explanation":"king → King. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: king → King. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Today we go to a big Park in the mountains.","options":[],"answer":"Today we go to a big park in the mountains.","explanation":"Park → park. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Park → park. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Tomorrow we visit jeddah.","options":[],"answer":"Tomorrow we visit Jeddah.","explanation":"jeddah → Jeddah. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: jeddah → Jeddah. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write about places.","items":[{"q":"Write the name of your city and your country.","options":[],"answer":"Taif, Saudi Arabia","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the name of a street, a park or a building you know.","options":[],"answer":"King Faisal Street","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about places you visit. Use one proper noun and one common noun.","options":[],"answer":"We visit Al-Rudaf Park. It is a big park with many trees.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"mosque","clue":"a building where Muslims pray"},{"word":"hospital","clue":"a building where doctors and nurses help sick people"},{"word":"library","clue":"a place with many books you can borrow"},{"word":"museum","clue":"a building where you can see old or interesting things"},{"word":"bakery","clue":"a shop that makes and sells bread and cakes"},{"word":"street","clue":"a road in a town with buildings on each side"},{"word":"bank","clue":"a place where people keep their money"},{"word":"supermarket","clue":"a big shop that sells food and other things"},{"word":"park","clue":"a public garden where people walk and play"},{"word":"corner","clue":"the place where two streets meet"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["I want to visit Madinah.","I Want to visit madinah.","i want to visit Madinah.","I want to visit madinah."],"answer":"I want to visit Madinah.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Find the word that needs a capital letter.","options":["street","jordan","city","park"],"answer":"jordan","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["The library is on rose street.","The library is on rose Street.","The library is on Rose Street.","The Library is on Rose street."],"answer":"The library is on Rose Street.","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["We live in a big City.","We live in a Big city.","We live in a big city.","we live in a big city."],"answer":"We live in a big city.","explanation":"General place words (street, city, park) are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["king Fahd Hospital","King fahd hospital","king fahd hospital","King Fahd Hospital"],"answer":"King Fahd Hospital","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How many capital letters are missing? \"my uncle lives in dammam.\"","options":["1","2","3","0"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["The mall is near taif museum.","The Mall is near Taif museum.","the mall is near taif Museum.","The mall is near Taif Museum."],"answer":"The mall is near Taif Museum.","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which word does NOT need a capital letter here? \"I like the ___ near my house.\"","options":["park","Taif","Saudi","King"],"answer":"park","explanation":"General place words (street, city, park) are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["kuwait is a small country.","Kuwait Is a small country.","Kuwait is a small country.","Kuwait is a small Country."],"answer":"Kuwait is a small country.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Our hotel is on Corniche Road in Jeddah.","Our hotel is on corniche road in jeddah.","Our hotel is on Corniche road in Jeddah.","Our Hotel is on Corniche Road in jeddah."],"answer":"Our hotel is on Corniche Road in Jeddah.","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Around My Town” that shows capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Around My Town” that shows capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings in action"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Capital Letters for Places”. Let’s learn capital letters for cities, countries, streets and named buildings together. A proper noun is the special name of one place. It starts with a capital letter: Taif, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, King Fahd Street, Al-Noor Mosque. A proper noun is the special name of one place. It starts with a capital letter: Taif, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, King Fahd Street, Al-Noor Mosque. A common noun is a general word: city, street, mosque, park. It does not need a capital letter: I live on a quiet street. Here are some examples. I live in Taif. My cousins live in Jeddah, near the sea. We go to King Abdullah Park on Friday. Be careful! Some learners say: “I live in taif.” That’s not right. We say: “I live in Taif.” City names need a capital letter. Quick check: Does \"street\" need a capital in \"I live on a long street\"? … Think! … No – it is a common noun. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Taif\", \"Saudi Arabia\" and \"King Fahd Street\" with capital letters.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5","title":"Welcome to My Town: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to ask for and give directions on a town map.","Students will be able to write a short guide to their town with directions and capital letters.","I can help a visitor find a place in my town.","I can write a short town guide."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من طلب الاتجاهات وإعطائها على خريطة المدينة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة دليل قصير لمدينتهم مع الاتجاهات والحروف الكبيرة.","أستطيع أن أساعد زائرًا على إيجاد مكان في مدينتي.","أستطيع أن أكتب دليلًا قصيرًا لمدينتي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mosque","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mɑsk/","definition":"a building where Muslims pray","arabic":"مسجد","example":"The mosque is next to our school.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hospital","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɑˌspɪtəl/","definition":"a building where doctors and nurses help sick people","arabic":"مستشفى","example":"My aunt works at the hospital.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bank","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bæŋk/","definition":"a place where people keep their money","arabic":"بنك / مصرف","example":"Dad goes to the bank on Sunday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bakery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbeɪkɚi/","definition":"a shop that makes and sells bread and cakes","arabic":"مخبز","example":"The bakery smells wonderful.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"supermarket","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsupɚˌmɑrkɪt/","definition":"a big shop that sells food and other things","arabic":"سوبرماركت","example":"We buy milk at the supermarket.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"park","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɑrk/","definition":"a public garden where people walk and play","arabic":"حديقة عامة","example":"Children play on the swings in the park.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"library","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlaɪbrɛˌri/","definition":"a place with many books you can borrow","arabic":"مكتبة عامة","example":"The library has a quiet reading room.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"museum","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mjuˈziəm/","definition":"a building where you can see old or interesting things","arabic":"متحف","example":"We see old coins at the museum.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bus stop","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bʌs stɑp/","definition":"a place where the bus stops for people","arabic":"موقف الحافلات","example":"Wait at the bus stop, please.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"street","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strit/","definition":"a road in a town with buildings on each side","arabic":"شارع","example":"Our street has tall palm trees.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"corner","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɔrnɚ/","definition":"the place where two streets meet","arabic":"زاوية / ناصية","example":"The pharmacy is on the corner.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"traffic light","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtræfɪk laɪt/","definition":"red, yellow and green lights that control cars","arabic":"إشارة المرور","example":"Stop at the red traffic light.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 3: directions with imperatives, prepositions of place, town words, questions for directions and capital letters for places.\nA town guide welcomes visitors, describes interesting places and helps people find them.\n✔ directions: Go straight, turn left/right, cross\n✔ between, opposite, near, on the corner, next to\n✔ Is there…? Where is…? How do I get to…?\n✔ capitals for city, street and building names","examples":["Welcome to Taif!","The flower market is on Shubra Street.","Turn right at the traffic light.","The museum is between the park and the mall.","Is there a good restaurant near here?","The bus stop is opposite the hospital.","Cross the street and walk past the bank.","How do I get to the old market?"],"common_errors":["✗ Welcome to taif! → ✓ Welcome to Taif! (City names need capitals.)","✗ You turn left and you go straight. → ✓ Turn left and go straight. (Directions: imperative, no you.)","✗ The park is opposite of the school. → ✓ The park is opposite the school. (No of after opposite.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الاتجاهات وحروف الجر وأماكن المدينة والحروف الكبيرة لأسماء الأماكن.\nالدليل السياحي يرحّب بالزائر ويصف الأماكن ويعطي الاتجاهات.\nلا نقول opposite of، بل opposite فقط."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Welcome to My Town: Language in Use”. Let’s learn directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U3-LS5 | Welcome to My Town: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Map game: Partner A chooses a place on the town map but keeps it secret. Partner B asks \"Is it near the park? Is it opposite the bank?\" Then Partner A gives directions from the school to the secret place.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 3: directions with imperatives, prepositions of place, town words, questions for directions and capital letters for places. A town guide welcomes visitors, describes interesting places and helps people find them.","on_screen":"✔ directions: Go straight, turn left/right, cross • ✔ between, opposite, near, on the corner, next to • ✔ Is there…? Where is…? How do I get to…?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Welcome to Taif! The flower market is on Shubra Street. Turn right at the traffic light.","on_screen":"Welcome to Taif! / The flower market is on Shubra Street. / Turn right at the traffic light.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Welcome to taif!.” That’s not right. We say: “Welcome to Taif!.” City names need capitals.","on_screen":"✗ Welcome to taif!   ✓ Welcome to Taif!","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “You turn left and you go straight.”? … Think! … It should be “Turn left and go straight.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can help a visitor find a place in my town.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can help a visitor find a place in my town.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الاتجاهات وحروف الجر وأماكن المدينة والحروف الكبيرة لأسماء الأماكن.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Welcome to taif! — الصحيح: Welcome to Taif!","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أساعد زائرًا على إيجاد مكان في مدينتي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Welcome to Taif! – Lina","body":"Welcome to Taif, the city of roses!\nAl-Rudaf Park is near the center. It has big rocks and green trees.\nThere is a famous rose farm on Al-Hada Road.\nTo get to the old market, go straight along King Faisal Street and turn left at the mosque. The market is opposite the bank.\nWe love our beautiful city!","word_count":58,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Lina's guide. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Taif is the city of roses.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Welcome to Taif! – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Al-Rudaf Park is far from the center.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Welcome to Taif! – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The rose farm is on Al-Hada Road.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Welcome to Taif! – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"To get to the old market, you turn right at the mosque.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Welcome to Taif! – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The market is opposite the bank.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Welcome to Taif! – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The park has big rocks and green trees.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Welcome to Taif! – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ left at the mosque.","options":["Turn","Turning","You turn","Turns"],"answer":"Turn","explanation":"Directions use imperatives: Go, Turn, Cross.","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"The market is ___ the bank. They face each other.","options":["in","between","opposite","under"],"answer":"opposite","explanation":"between … and • opposite • near • on the corner.","explanation_ar":"حروف الجر للمكان."},{"q":"Excuse me, ___ a bakery near here?","options":["have","there is","is there","are there"],"answer":"is there","explanation":"Where is…? / Is there…? / How do I get to…?","explanation_ar":"أسئلة الاتجاهات."},{"q":"We buy medicine at the ___.","options":["library","pharmacy","museum","bakery"],"answer":"pharmacy","explanation":"Choose the right town word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المكان الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["we drive on King Faisal street.","We drive on king faisal street.","We drive on King faisal street.","We drive on King Faisal Street."],"answer":"We drive on King Faisal Street.","explanation":"Place names start with capital letters.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأماكن بحرف كبير."},{"q":"The café is ___ the corner.","options":["in","on","between","opposite"],"answer":"on","explanation":"between … and • opposite • near • on the corner.","explanation_ar":"حروف الجر للمكان."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Map game. Write the questions and answers.","items":[{"q":"Ask about the secret place with \"Is it near…?\"","options":[],"answer":"Is it near the park?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask with \"Is it opposite…?\"","options":[],"answer":"Is it opposite the hospital?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask with \"Is it between…?\"","options":[],"answer":"Is it between the bank and the bakery?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Guess the place.","options":[],"answer":"Is it the library?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the directions your partner gives you.","options":[],"answer":"Go straight, turn right at the bank, and the library is on the left.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your town guide.","items":[{"q":"Plan: your town's name and 3 places to visit.","options":[],"answer":"Taif – Al-Rudaf Park, the rose farm, the old market","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 5–6 sentences. Give directions to one place.","options":[],"answer":"Welcome to Taif! Al-Rudaf Park is near the center. The rose farm is on Al-Hada Road. To get to the market, go straight and turn left at the mosque. It is opposite the bank.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: capital letters for names? imperatives? prepositions? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"al-hada road\" to \"Al-Hada Road\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"mosque","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hospital","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bank","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bakery","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"supermarket","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"park","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"library","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"museum","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bus stop","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"street","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"corner","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"traffic light","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ the street at the traffic light.","options":["Crossing","You crosses","Crosses","Cross"],"answer":"Cross","explanation":"Directions use imperatives: Go, Turn, Cross.","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"The bank is ___ the café and the shop.","options":["opposite","in front","under","between"],"answer":"between","explanation":"between … and • opposite • near • on the corner.","explanation_ar":"حروف الجر للمكان."},{"q":"","options":["Excuse me, how do I gets to the museum?","Excuse me, how I get to the museum?","Excuse me, how do I get to the museum?","Excuse me, how do get I to the museum?"],"answer":"Excuse me, how do I get to the museum?","explanation":"Where is…? / Is there…? / How do I get to…?","explanation_ar":"أسئلة الاتجاهات."},{"q":"People pray at the ___.","options":["post office","bank","bakery","mosque"],"answer":"mosque","explanation":"Choose the right town word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المكان الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["I live near al-noor mosque in jeddah.","I live near Al-Noor Mosque in Jeddah.","I live near Al-Noor mosque in jeddah.","i live near Al-Noor Mosque in Jeddah."],"answer":"I live near Al-Noor Mosque in Jeddah.","explanation":"Place names start with capital letters.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأماكن بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Is there a bus stop near the school? – Yes, ___.","options":["there is","it is","there are","is there"],"answer":"there is","explanation":"Where is…? / Is there…? / How do I get to…?","explanation_ar":"أسئلة الاتجاهات."},{"q":"The park is ___ the hospital.","options":["opposite","in front","opposite of","between of"],"answer":"opposite","explanation":"between … and • opposite • near • on the corner.","explanation_ar":"حروف الجر للمكان."},{"q":"","options":["Goes straight and turns right at the bakery.","Go straight and turn right at the bakery.","You go straight and you turn right at the bakery.","Go straight and turn to right at the bakery."],"answer":"Go straight and turn right at the bakery.","explanation":"Directions use imperatives: Go, Turn, Cross.","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"We borrow books at the ___.","options":["bakery","supermarket","library","bank"],"answer":"library","explanation":"Choose the right town word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المكان الصحيحة."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a town guide:","options":["The Museum is near king Fahd park.","The museum is near king fahd park.","The museum is near King Fahd Park.","The museum near is King Fahd Park."],"answer":"The museum is near King Fahd Park.","explanation":"Place names start with capital letters.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأماكن بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Lina and Noura making a \"Welcome to Taif\" guide with a hand-drawn map, roses and the mountains in the background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Lina and Noura making a \"Welcome to Taif\" guide with a hand-drawn map, roses and the mountains in the background"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Around My Town”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Around My Town”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L02-U3-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS5-T1","script":"Welcome to Taif, the city of roses! Al-Rudaf Park is near the center. It has big rocks and green trees. There is a famous rose farm on Al-Hada Road. To get to the old market, go straight along King Faisal Street and turn left at the mosque. The market is opposite the bank. We love our beautiful city!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U3-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Welcome to My Town: Language in Use”. Let’s learn directions, prepositions, places in town and capital letters for places (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Map game: Partner A chooses a place on the town map but keeps it secret. Partner B asks \"Is it near the park? Is it opposite the bank?\" Then Partner A gives directions from the school to the secret place. Today you use all of Unit 3: directions with imperatives, prepositions of place, town words, questions for directions and capital letters for places. A town guide welcomes visitors, describes interesting places and helps people find them. Here are some examples. Welcome to Taif! The flower market is on Shubra Street. Turn right at the traffic light. Be careful! Some learners say: “Welcome to taif!.” That’s not right. We say: “Welcome to Taif!.” City names need capitals. Quick check: what is wrong with “You turn left and you go straight.”? … Think! … It should be “Turn left and go straight.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can help a visitor find a place in my town.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"The pharmacy is ___ the bakery and the bank.","options":["in","under","between","opposite"],"answer":"between","explanation":"between A and B.","explanation_ar":"between ثم المكان الأول ثم and ثم الثاني."},{"q":"The school is ___ the park. They face each other.","options":["under","in","between","opposite"],"answer":"opposite","explanation":"opposite / across from = facing on the other side.","explanation_ar":"opposite تعني مقابل."},{"q":"___ straight for three blocks.","options":["Go","You goes","Going","Goes"],"answer":"Go","explanation":"Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["You turning left at the traffic light.","Turn left at the traffic light.","Turn to left at the traffic light.","Turns left at the traffic light."],"answer":"Turn left at the traffic light.","explanation":"Turn left/right – no to.","explanation_ar":"نقول Turn left بدون to."},{"q":"The flower shop is ___ the corner.","options":["in","on","under","between"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on the corner = where two streets meet.","explanation_ar":"on the corner تعني على الزاوية."},{"q":"___, is there a hospital near here?","options":["Excuse me","Thank you","Goodbye","You're welcome"],"answer":"Excuse me","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."},{"q":"","options":["Is there a mosque on this street?","Have a mosque on this street?","There is a mosque on this street?","Is a mosque there on this street?"],"answer":"Is there a mosque on this street?","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."},{"q":"","options":["Where the bus stop is?","The bus stop where is?","Where is the bus stop?","Where is bus stop the?"],"answer":"Where is the bus stop?","explanation":"Where is + place?","explanation_ar":"Where is ثم المكان."},{"q":"How do I get ___ the park?","options":["at","on","in","to"],"answer":"to","explanation":"How do I get to + place?","explanation_ar":"How do I get to للسؤال عن الطريق."},{"q":"Thanks for your help! – ___","options":["Excuse me.","You're welcome.","Turn right.","Yes, there is."],"answer":"You're welcome.","explanation":"Start with Excuse me; end with Thank you / You're welcome.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بـ Excuse me وأنهِ بالشكر."},{"q":"Nurses take care of sick people at the ___.","options":["bakery","museum","hospital","bank"],"answer":"hospital","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"We buy bread at the ___.","options":["library","bank","bakery","post office"],"answer":"bakery","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"The big red fire trucks wait at the ___.","options":["station fire","police office","bus stop","fire station"],"answer":"fire station","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"We ___ books from the library.","options":["pay","buy","borrow","sell"],"answer":"borrow","explanation":"borrow = take and give back later; buy = pay money.","explanation_ar":"borrow تعني يستعير."},{"q":"Find the compound noun.","options":["city","post office","post","office"],"answer":"post office","explanation":"In a compound noun, the \"kind\" word comes first.","explanation_ar":"في الاسم المركب كلمة النوع أولًا."},{"q":"The call to prayer comes from the ___.","options":["bank","museum","bakery","mosque"],"answer":"mosque","explanation":"Choose the place that matches what people do there.","explanation_ar":"اختر المكان المناسب للنشاط."},{"q":"","options":["My grandparents live in abha.","My Grandparents live in abha.","My grandparents live in Abha.","my grandparents live in Abha"],"answer":"My grandparents live in Abha.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["The shop is on Rose Street.","The shop is on Rose street.","The shop is on rose street.","The Shop is on rose Street."],"answer":"The shop is on Rose Street.","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["There is a big park in our City.","There is a big park in our city.","there is a big park in our city.","There is a big Park in our City."],"answer":"There is a big park in our city.","explanation":"General place words (street, city, park) are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"How many capital letters are missing? \"we visit madinah in summer.\"","options":["2","3","1","0"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["king Abdullah Park","King abdullah park","king abdullah park","King Abdullah Park"],"answer":"King Abdullah Park","explanation":"Every main word in a place name has a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"كل كلمة في اسم المكان بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a visitor's guide:","options":["The bakery is opposite of al-noor mosque.","The bakery opposite is Al-Noor Mosque.","The Bakery is opposite al-Noor mosque.","The bakery is opposite Al-Noor Mosque."],"answer":"The bakery is opposite Al-Noor Mosque.","explanation":"opposite / across from = facing on the other side.","explanation_ar":"opposite تعني مقابل."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"you go straight and you turn left.\"","options":["You go straight and turn left.","Go straight and turn left.","Goes straight and turns left.","go straight and you turn left."],"answer":"Go straight and turn left.","explanation":"Directions: base verb at the start (Go, Turn, Cross).","explanation_ar":"الاتجاهات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"Is there a bank near here? – ___","options":["No, there isn't.","No, it isn't there.","No, there aren't.","No, isn't there."],"answer":"No, there isn't.","explanation":"Is there a/an … near here? – Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","explanation_ar":"Is there للسؤال عن وجود مكان."}],"theme_ar":"في مدينتي","essential_question_ar":"كيف نجد طريقنا ونساعد الآخرين في مدينتنا؟","can_do":"I can ask for and give simple directions and describe where places are in my town.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أطلب الاتجاهات وأعطيها، وأصف أماكن المباني في مدينتي."});
